T Axle in a bearing
# A rod through a connector's centre hole is the only true bearing in the system: it spins and it
# slides. Spacers either side of each hub stop the sliding; end caps stop the rod walking out.
! two posts
C P1 W8 -2,0,0.5 x y
C P2 W8 2,0,0.5 x y
C Q1 W8 -2,0,2.5 x y
C Q2 W8 2,0,2.5 x y
R P1 Q1
R P2 Q2
! the axle, capped, with the spinning wheel hub parked by spacers
R -2.828,0,2.5 2.828,0,2.5 grey
C CL D1 -2.828,0,2.5 y x
C CR D1 2.828,0,2.5 y -x
H WHEEL W8 0,0,2.5 z
P -0.2,0,2.5 silver
P 0.2,0,2.5 silver
